{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310795,"nonce":"1wPv0PFttGrjGv6yGNLpTag3org=","title":"Comprehensive per-kernel decode breakdown after instrumenting 10 previously-uninstrumented externs at commit 039445e. 99.9% accounted for; ...","message":"Decode-wall budget on 80-tok canonical \"Write a short poem about the sea\"\n(2.22 s wall, ~36 tok/s on M1 Pro, llvm-backend + profile build):\n\n| Kernel | Wall | % | Calls | µs/call |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| matmul_qt_t_f32_threaded | 1896 ms | **86.9%** | 7233 | 262 |\n| matmul_qkv_qt_t_f32_threaded | 90 ms | 4.1% | 1296 | 70 |\n| topk_scan | 84 ms | 3.9% | 81 | 1043 |\n| flash_attn_decode | 51 ms | 2.3% | 1280 | 40 |\n| tensor_silu | 24 ms | 1.1% | 1296 | 19 |\n| tensor_rope | 12 ms | 0.6% | 2592 | 5 |\n| tensor_rms_norm | 7 ms | 0.3% | 2673 | 3 |\n| tensor_free | 7 ms | 0.3% | 37785 | 0.19 |\n| tensor_reshape | 6 ms | 0.3% | 5265 | 1 |\n| tensor_add_into | 1.7 ms | 0.1% | 2592 | 0.6 |\n| tensor_softmax | 0.4 ms | 0.0% | 16 | 25 |\n| tensor_clone | 0.3 ms | 0.0% | 12433 | 0.027 |\n\nTotal instrumented = 99.9%. The \"257 ms unattributed pure Haxe\norchestration\" framing from the per-phase profile was overstated; most\nof that gap was prefill-time kernel calls that the per-phase profile\ndoesn't include (prefill happens before the decode loop body).\n\n\nThis breakdown REFUTES several hypotheses raised during the wjxvc4laa\nworkflow's synthesis:\n\n- **ArcCloneElisionPass (forecast 6.5% on real decode)**: actual ceiling\n  is `tensor_clone + tensor_free combined = 7.3 ms = 0.3% of decode`.\n  Forecast was off by ~20x; pass would have washed out for the 6th\n  time this session.\n- **TensorPoolFastPath (forecast 3%)**: `tensor_free` at 188 ns/call\n  is already at uncontended-pool speed; TLS freelist saves ~20 ns/call,\n  so 37785 × 20 ns = 0.76 ms = 0.03%. Refuted.\n- **EscapeAnalysis LICM hoist of clones (forecast 1.5%)**: with clone\n  at 27 ns and total 0.3 ms, even complete hoisting saves nothing\n  measurable. Refuted.\n- **DevirtualizationPass Array\u003cInterface\u003e narrowing (forecast 0.1%)**:\n  the standalone bench at `compiler/benchmarks/src/orchestration_overhead.hx`\n  showed dispatch is 155 ns/layer-iter = 1300× under the 200 µs/layer\n  budget. Refuted independently.\n\n\nThe matmul_qt_t kernel at 86.9% is already at M1's ILP saturation point\n(per `bugs_q4km_4block_paired_no_win` — the 4-block paired SDOT washed\nout 2026-06-07; M1 OoO scheduler tops out at ~8 in-flight SDOTs which\n2-block already hits).\n\nOther kernels each \u003c 5%; the only ones above 1% are:\n- topk_scan (3.9%) — already NEON-SIMD optimised at 3730292\n- tensor_silu (1.1%) — could be fused with up/gate matmul (SwiGLU\n  fusion was tried at bugs_swiglu_fusion_no_win and washed out -0.2%)\n\nThere is no remaining double-digit lever on this model/hardware\nwithout an algorithmic restructure (speculative decoding, larger batch,\ndifferent quantisation).\n\n\nThe wjxvc4laa workflow's \"synth + 2 adversarial verifiers\" pattern was\nload-bearing. The synth proposed a 6.5% forecast based on fabricated\nper-FFI-cost arithmetic; both verifiers independently identified the\nsame flaw (unverified 30 µs anchor vs actual ~2-30 ns measurable in\ncode) and recommended the SAME 30-minute instrumentation experiment\n(extend kernel_timing.rs) before any pass work. The instrumentation\ntook ~20 minutes and saved 14-32 engineer-hours of speculative pass\nwork that would have washed out.\n\nPattern: when forecast hinges on an unverified primitive cost,\ninstrument-first dominates implement-first.\n\n\n- [[perf-kernel-breakdown-2026-06-07]] — earlier partial breakdown (9 kernels)\n- [[bugs-q4km-4block-paired-no-win]] — matmul saturation evidence\n- [[bugs-swiglu-fusion-no-win]] — silu+up fusion already tried\n- [[perf-topk-scan-neon-simd]] — topk already optimised\n- [[bugs-forkjoin-atomic-countdown-no-win]] — wash-out streak context\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_kernel_breakdown_full_2026_06_07` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}